        whyItMatters:
          "Whether an appeal can revisit factual findings or only legal questions depends structurally on which track actually applies, and a party expecting a full factual re-examination on Revision will be disappointed, since that track is deliberately limited to legal error review and will not reconsider whether the trial court correctly weighed the underlying evidence. You should always identify, at the very start of any appeal, which originating court produced the judgment being challenged, since that single fact determines the entire available appellate track, full factual re-examination through Berufung, or narrower legal review through Revision, before any substantive argument about the case itself even becomes relevant.",
