        whyItMatters:
          "Human dignity plays a structurally central, almost foundational role in German constitutional reasoning that has no precise parallel in US constitutional doctrine, which does not organize its rights framework around one supreme, explicitly foundational value in the same way. You should always ask, when analyzing any German fundamental-rights question, whether human dignity is genuinely implicated as an independent, non-derogable floor, since a right that might otherwise yield to a sufficiently weighty government interest under the proportionality test covered later in this lecture simply cannot be balanced away at all once Article 1 itself is actually engaged.",
